    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "# Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Four routines, each doing one job.\n",
    "\n",
    "**`sweep()`** is the workhorse: step the generator across a list of frequencies, keep the\n",
    "receiver pinned exactly on the drive, and read a complex number at each point. Only its\n",
    "**magnitude** is used. The phase is returned but is not a measurement — the two oscillators are\n",
    "retuned by separate register writes, and the gap between them puts an uncontrolled and jittery\n",
    "phase on every point.\n",
    "\n",
    "**`fit_lorentzian()`** turns amplitude-versus-frequency into a centre and a width. The trick\n",
    "that makes it need no fitting library: the *reciprocal* of a Lorentzian power curve is a\n",
    "parabola in frequency, so an ordinary weighted quadratic fit recovers everything. The\n",
    "complication it has to handle is a **baseline**. `1/p` is a parabola only for a *pure*\n",
    "Lorentzian; any additive floor is absorbed into the parabola and inflates the fitted width —\n",
    "negligible where the peak towers over the floor, severe where it does not. On a bench coil\n",
    "behind 0.3 pF the floor will not be negligible, so the baseline is found by search rather than\n",
    "assumed to be zero.\n",
    "\n",
    "**`fit_lorentzian()`** is the classical fit: a symmetric Lorentzian plus a flat power floor.\n",
    "Correct whenever the background adds *incoherently*.\n",
    "\n",
    "**`fit_fano()`** is the one everything now uses. It adds the antisymmetric term that a coherent\n",
    "leak produces by interference, which a symmetric fit cannot represent and instead absorbs as\n",
    "extra width. It is linear in its three amplitudes for any trial centre and width, so only two\n",
    "numbers are searched — and, unlike its predecessor, it **checks whether the search stopped at\n",
    "the edge of its own grid and refuses rather than reporting the edge as a measurement**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**`fit_or_raise()`** turns a refusal into an exception carrying the reason. Every caller here\n",
    "wants either a number it can trust or a loud failure; quietly substituting a grid boundary for a\n",
    "measurement is how a coil of unchanged quality factor came back as 672 and then 2499.\n",
    "\n",
    "All of these work on `|z|²` alone. Nothing in this notebook uses the phase *between* sweep\n",
    "points — see the note above Step 5 for why that is not available on this board.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  ANALYSIS\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "def sweep(freqs, drive_frac=None, navg=None, settle=None, level_guard=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Drive at each frequency and read the complex response at DC.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns (f_actual, z) where f_actual is what the generator really produced\n",
    "    (its word is quantised) and z is complex - amplitude AND phase.\n",
    "\n",
    "    The receiver is tuned by WORD, not by hertz, so the signal lands at exactly\n",
    "    zero frequency and the two register reads cannot land on different phases of\n",
    "    a rotating vector.\"\"\"\n",
    "    drive_frac = DRIVE_FRAC if drive_frac is None else drive_frac\n",
    "    navg = N_AVG if navg is None else navg\n",
    "    settle = SETTLE if settle is None else settle\n",
    "\n",
    "    gen.amp(drive_frac)                  # refused outright if above DRIVE_MAX\n",
    "    gen.run()\n",
    "    f_act = np.zeros(len(freqs))\n",
    "    z = np.zeros(len(freqs), dtype=complex)\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        for k, f in enumerate(freqs):\n",
    "            f_act[k] = gen.freq(f)\n",
    "            acq.tune_word(gen.lo_word())\n",
    "            time.sleep(settle)\n",
    "            if level_guard is not None and sc.peak_frac(GUARD_NSAMP) > level_guard:\n",
    "                raise RuntimeError('input exceeded %.0f%% of full scale at %.6f MHz'\n",
    "                                   % (100 * level_guard, f_act[k] / 1e6))\n",
    "            z[k] = acq.measure(navg)\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        # Whatever ended this sweep - the guard above, a bad register read, a\n",
    "        # Ctrl-C halfway through a 350-point pass - the drive comes off. This is\n",
    "        # the single most important line in the notebook: every measurement goes\n",
    "        # through here, so no failure path can walk away leaving the coil driven.\n",
    "        gen.amp(0.0)\n",
    "    return f_act, z\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def fit_lorentzian(f, p, guard=0.05, minpts=5):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Centre, linewidth, peak and baseline from power p against frequency f.\n",
    "\n",
    "    1/p is a parabola in f for a PURE Lorentzian. Any additive floor is absorbed\n",
    "    into that parabola and widens the answer, so the floor is found by search:\n",
    "    for each trial floor, subtract it, fit, rebuild the full model, and keep the\n",
    "    trial that reproduces the measured points best. Two passes, coarse then fine.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Points below `guard` of the peak are excluded - their reciprocals are all\n",
    "    noise - and the rest are weighted by their power, so the well-measured points\n",
    "    near the top dominate.\"\"\"\n",
    "    f = np.asarray(f, dtype=float)\n",
    "    p = np.asarray(p, dtype=float)\n",
    "    pmax = float(np.max(p))\n",
    "    u = f - f.mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "    def _try(b):\n",
    "        q = p - b\n",
    "        keep = q > guard * q.max()\n",
    "        if int(np.count_nonzero(keep)) < minpts:\n",
    "            return None\n",
    "        A, B, C = np.polyfit(u[keep], 1.0 / q[keep], 2, w=q[keep])\n",
    "        if A <= 0.0:\n",
    "            return None                              # parabola opens the wrong way\n",
    "        u0 = -B / (2.0 * A)\n",
    "        lw = 2.0 * np.sqrt(max(C / A - u0 ** 2, 1e-30))\n",
    "        p0 = 1.0 / max(C - A * u0 ** 2, 1e-300)\n",
    "        f0 = f.mean() + u0\n",
    "        model = p0 / (1.0 + (2.0 * (f - f0) / lw) ** 2) + b\n",
    "        rms = float(np.sqrt(np.mean(((p - model) / pmax) ** 2)))\n",
    "        return rms, (f0, lw, p0, b)\n",
    "\n",
    "    best, best_b = _try(0.0), 0.0\n",
    "    hi = 0.999 * float(np.min(p))\n",
    "    if hi > 0.0:\n",
    "        for b in np.linspace(0.0, hi, 17):\n",
    "            got = _try(b)\n",
    "            if got is not None and (best is None or got[0] < best[0]):\n",
    "                best, best_b = got, b\n",
    "        w = hi / 16.0\n",
    "        for b in np.linspace(max(best_b - w, 0.0), min(best_b + w, hi), 17):\n",
    "            got = _try(b)\n",
    "            if got is not None and (best is None or got[0] < best[0]):\n",
    "                best, best_b = got, b\n",
    "    if best is None:\n",
    "        raise ValueError('fit failed: only %d points above the guard'\n",
    "                         % int(np.count_nonzero(p > guard * p.max())))\n",
    "    resid = best[0]\n",
    "    f0, lw, p0, base = best[1]\n",
    "    return dict(f0=f0, lw=lw, peak=p0, base=base, resid=resid, Q=f0 / lw)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def fit_fano(f, p, f0_hint, lw_hint, n_f0=41, n_lw=61, passes=5,\n",
    "             span_f0=1.5, span_lw=1.6, max_expand=3):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Asymmetric (Fano) lineshape fitted to POWER. Uses no phase information.\n",
    "\n",
    "    THE MODEL.  A coherent leak reaching the input interferes with the coil's\n",
    "    response, so the power is\n",
    "\n",
    "        |A/(1+ix) + B e^{i th}|^2\n",
    "            = B^2  +  (A^2 + 2AB cos th)/(1+x^2)  +  (2AB sin th) x/(1+x^2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    with x = 2(f-f0)/lw.  Written that way it is\n",
    "\n",
    "        P(f) = base + C1/(1+x^2) + C2 x/(1+x^2)\n",
    "\n",
    "    which is LINEAR in (base, C1, C2) for any trial (f0, lw).  So the three\n",
    "    amplitudes come from a 3x3 solve and only two numbers are ever searched.\n",
    "    The C2 term is the interference: it is the antisymmetric part, it is what a\n",
    "    symmetric Lorentzian cannot represent, and it is what inflates the width of\n",
    "    a fit that lacks it.  A, B and the leak phase are recovered afterwards.\n",
    "\n",
    "    WHY NOT FIT THE COMPLEX RESPONSE.  Because the phase between one sweep point\n",
    "    and the next is not trustworthy on this board - see the note above Step 5.\n",
    "    Everything here uses |z|^2 only, which is immune to that.\n",
    "\n",
    "    RAILS.  A grid search that stops at the edge of its grid has not measured\n",
    "    anything; it has reported the edge.  Each pass therefore checks whether the\n",
    "    best point sits on a boundary and EXPANDS rather than shrinks if so.  If it\n",
    "    is still on a boundary after `max_expand` expansions the fit REFUSES, with a\n",
    "    reason, instead of returning the boundary as though it were an answer.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    f = np.asarray(f, dtype=float)\n",
    "    p = np.asarray(p, dtype=float)\n",
    "    n = len(f)\n",
    "    if n < 8:\n",
    "        return None, 'only %d points - too few to fit' % n\n",
    "    pn = float(np.sum((p - p.mean()) ** 2))\n",
    "\n",
    "    def scan(f0s, lws):\n",
    "        \"\"\"Best (cost, f0, lw, coeffs) over the grid, vectorised across f0.\"\"\"\n",
    "        best = None\n",
    "        bi = bj = -1\n",
    "        for j, lw in enumerate(lws):\n",
    "            x = 2.0 * (f[None, :] - f0s[:, None]) / lw          # (n_f0, n)\n",
    "            d = 1.0 / (1.0 + x * x)\n",
    "            B = np.empty(x.shape + (3,))\n",
    "            B[:, :, 0] = 1.0\n",
    "            B[:, :, 1] = d\n",
    "            B[:, :, 2] = x * d\n",
    "            G = np.einsum('ijk,ijl->ikl', B, B)\n",
    "            y = np.einsum('ijk,j->ik', B, p)\n",
    "            G = G + np.eye(3)[None, :, :] * 1e-12 * np.trace(G, axis1=1, axis2=2)[:, None, None]\n",
    "            try:\n",
    "                # y[..., None] keeps this a STACK of 3-vectors. Passing a 2-D y\n",
    "                # makes numpy read it as one matrix and the shapes collide.\n",
    "                c = np.linalg.solve(G, y[:, :, None])[:, :, 0]\n",
    "            except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            r = p[None, :] - np.einsum('ijk,ik->ij', B, c)\n",
    "            cost = np.sum(r * r, axis=1)\n",
    "            k = int(np.argmin(cost))\n",
    "            if best is None or cost[k] < best[0]:\n",
    "                best = (float(cost[k]), float(f0s[k]), float(lw), c[k].copy())\n",
    "                bi, bj = k, j\n",
    "        return best, bi, bj\n",
    "\n",
    "    f0c, lwc = float(f0_hint), float(lw_hint)\n",
    "    sf, sl = float(span_f0), float(span_lw)\n",
    "    expands = 0\n",
    "    best = None\n",
    "    for _ in range(passes + max_expand):\n",
    "        f0s = f0c + np.linspace(-sf, sf, n_f0) * lw_hint\n",
    "        lws = lwc * np.exp(np.linspace(-sl, sl, n_lw))\n",
    "        best, bi, bj = scan(f0s, lws)\n",
    "        if best is None:\n",
    "            return None, 'the linear solve failed everywhere on the grid'\n",
    "        railed = (bi in (0, n_f0 - 1)) or (bj in (0, n_lw - 1))\n",
    "        f0c, lwc = best[1], best[2]\n",
    "        if railed:\n",
    "            expands += 1\n",
    "            if expands > max_expand:\n",
    "                which = 'centre' if bi in (0, n_f0 - 1) else 'width'\n",
    "                return None, ('the %s ran to the edge of the search on %d '\n",
    "                              'successive expansions (last width tried: %.1f to '\n",
    "                              '%.1f kHz). The line is not where the hint says it '\n",
    "                              'is, or the shape is not a resonance at all'\n",
    "                              % (which, expands, lws[0] / 1e3, lws[-1] / 1e3))\n",
    "            sf *= 2.0\n",
    "            sl *= 1.5\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            sf /= 3.0\n",
    "            sl /= 3.0\n",
    "\n",
    "    cost, f0, lw, (base, c1, c2) = best\n",
    "    if lw <= 0 or not np.isfinite(lw) or c1 <= 0:\n",
    "        return None, 'the fitted width or peak is not a positive number'\n",
    "\n",
    "    resid = float(np.sqrt(cost / max(pn, 1e-300)))\n",
    "    rms = float(np.sqrt(cost / n))\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ---- refuse a fit that has not actually found a resonance ----------------\n",
    "    #  A grid search always returns its best point, and on featureless data that\n",
    "    #  point is meaningless. Two tests, both cheap: does the model explain the\n",
    "    #  variation at all, and is the resonant term big next to the scatter?\n",
    "    if resid > 0.7:\n",
    "        return None, ('the model explains almost none of the variation '\n",
    "                      '(residual %.2f of the record) - this is not a resonance'\n",
    "                      % resid)\n",
    "    if abs(c1) < 4.0 * rms:\n",
    "        return None, ('the resonant term is only %.1fx the point scatter - '\n",
    "                      'nothing here is significantly above the noise'\n",
    "                      % (abs(c1) / max(rms, 1e-300)))\n",
    "\n",
    "    # ---- what power alone CAN and CANNOT tell you ----------------------------\n",
    "    #  base is the leak power, unambiguously: it is the floor far from the line.\n",
    "    #  Splitting the on-resonance response into resonator and leak amplitudes,\n",
    "    #  though, needs the relative phase, and |z|^2 does not carry it - the\n",
    "    #  quadratic below has two positive roots that fit the data equally well.\n",
    "    #  So the split is NOT reported. What is reported is the ratio that is well\n",
    "    #  defined either way, and is exactly what Step 4 measures directly:\n",
    "    #\n",
    "    #      leak_frac = |leak| / |response on resonance|\n",
    "    #\n",
    "    on_res = float(base + c1)                       # power at the line centre\n",
    "    amp_leak = float(np.sqrt(max(base, 0.0)))\n",
    "    amp_on = float(np.sqrt(max(on_res, 1e-300)))\n",
    "    return dict(f0=f0, lw=lw, Q=f0 / lw,\n",
    "                peak=float(c1), base=float(max(base, 0.0)),\n",
    "                amp_leak=amp_leak, amp_on=amp_on,\n",
    "                leak_frac=float(min(amp_leak / amp_on, 1.0)),\n",
    "                asym=float(c2 / max(abs(c1), 1e-300)),\n",
    "                c1=float(c1), c2=float(c2), resid=resid), None\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def fit_or_raise(f, p, f0_hint, lw_hint, what='fit'):\n",
    "    \"\"\"fit_fano(), but a refusal becomes an exception with the reason attached.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Every caller in this notebook wants one of two things: a number it can\n",
    "    trust, or a loud failure. Silently substituting a grid boundary for a\n",
    "    measurement is what produced quality factors of 672 and 2499 out of a coil\n",
    "    that had not changed.\"\"\"\n",
    "    got, why = fit_fano(f, p, f0_hint, lw_hint)\n",
    "    if got is None:\n",
    "        raise ValueError('%s refused: %s' % (what, why))\n",
    "    return got\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "print('analysis helpers defined')"
   ]
  },
