    "---\n",
    "# Step 2 — Levels, and what else is in the band\n",
    "\n",
    "Three questions from one set of measurements, because they are really the same question:\n",
    "**can I trust what I am being given?**\n",
    "\n",
    "| | Why it matters |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Are the levels sane? | An overloaded input produces a distorted shape that still looks vaguely like a resonance. This project's signature failure |\n",
    "| What else is in the band? | A clock harmonic near the coil's frequency would be found by Step 3's search and fitted as a spectacular high-quality-factor resonance |\n",
    "| How quiet is the input? | The floor decides whether a resonance is findable at all, and whether Step 4 will need an amplifier |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Run this with the input terminated first.** That catalogues the board's *own* stray signals —\n",
    "switching-supply harmonics, clock spurs, the generator's own leakage. Then run it again with\n",
    "the coil attached, and anything new belongs to the coil or to the room. Without the first run\n",
    "there is no way to tell those apart.\n",
    "\n",
    "The survey steps the receiver across the band with the generator **off** and records the power\n",
    "in each window. It is deliberately coarse: it is looking for things that should not be there,\n",
    "not measuring them."
   ]
  },
