   "source": [
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "# Step 3 — Find the resonance without being told where it is\n",
    "\n",
    "Everything from Stage 8 upward has been *handed* the answer, and about forty places downstream\n",
    "read it back. Here there is nothing to hand over. Three widening passes:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Pass | What it does | Why that way |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **Look around** | Step across the whole plausible band, few averages, no fitting | It only has to find the neighbourhood. Nothing is fitted, so there is nothing to be fooled by |\n",
    "| **Bracket** | Widen around the best candidate until the curve clearly comes back down on *both* sides | A fit interpolating between points is trustworthy; one extrapolating past them is not |\n",
    "| **Refine** | A dense sweep at a decimation chosen from the width just estimated, then fit | The receiver window must be small next to the linewidth or the window smears the curve |\n",
    "\n",
    "**`SEARCH_STEP` is the parameter that decides whether this works.** The coarse pass cannot find\n",
    "a line narrower than its own step — it walks straight over it. If nothing is found, halve the\n",
    "step before doing anything else.\n",
    "\n",
    "The receiver is retuned to each drive frequency, so the response is always read at zero\n",
    "frequency. That is why the coarse pass can be quick and still be exact."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  STEP 3 - FIND THE RESONANCE\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "def choose_dec(lw):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Pick log2(decimation) so the receiver window is small next to a linewidth.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Aim: clean half-window <= lw/10, i.e. 0.1 x output_rate <= lw/10, i.e.\n",
    "    output_rate <= lw. Clamped to 8..12, because below R = 256 the droop\n",
    "    corrector bypasses itself and above R = 4096 the hardware stops.\"\"\"\n",
    "    d = int(np.ceil(np.log2(FS_CLK / max(lw, 1.0))))\n",
    "    return int(min(12, max(8, d)))\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def half_power_width(f, p):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Crude width straight off the data: the span above half the peak.\n",
    "\n",
    "    Deliberately not a fit. Used only to decide how wide the next sweep should\n",
    "    be, where being fooled by a fit would be worse than being approximate.\"\"\"\n",
    "    p = np.asarray(p, dtype=float)\n",
    "    base = float(np.median(p))\n",
    "    half = base + 0.5 * (float(np.max(p)) - base)\n",
    "    above = np.where(p >= half)[0]\n",
    "    if len(above) < 2:\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    return float(f[above[-1]] - f[above[0]])\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "if not COIL_CONNECTED:\n",
    "    raise SystemExit('COIL_CONNECTED is False - Steps 3 onwards need the coil. '\n",
    "                     'Stop here; the survey above is the deliverable for this run.')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "print('STEP 3 - find the resonance')\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "\n",
    "emu.disable()\n",
