    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "# Step 4 — What the 0.3 pF coupling actually costs\n",
    "\n",
    "Two numbers, one predicted and one measured, and they should roughly agree. Where they do not,\n",
    "the difference is telling you something about the wiring rather than the coil.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The prediction.** The pickup capacitor and everything after it — cable, connector, board\n",
    "input — form a capacitive divider. 0.3 pF against 30 pF of cable divides by about a hundred.\n",
    "The reactance of 0.3 pF at 40 MHz is around 13 kΩ, which is the *good* half of the trade: it\n",
    "means almost nothing is drawn from the tank, so the quality factor you measured in Step 3\n",
    "should be close to the coil's own.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The measurement.** How much signal actually arrived, in counts and in volts, against the\n",
    "noise floor from Step 2. That ratio decides whether an amplifier is needed.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The practical conclusion, in advance:** *driven* measurements — everything in this notebook —\n",
    "generally work without an amplifier, because you can simply drive harder. What needs one is\n",
    "anything driven by the coil's **own thermal noise**, which is how the real experiment works.\n",
    "If `L_EST` is supplied, the last block estimates that directly."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  STEP 4 - SIGNAL BUDGET\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "print('STEP 4 - what the coupling costs')\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "\n",
    "w0 = 2.0 * np.pi * F0\n",
    "Xc = 1.0 / (w0 * C_COUPLE)\n",
    "divider = C_COUPLE / (C_COUPLE + C_STRAY_EST)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('PREDICTED, from the values in the configuration cell')\n",
    "print('  reactance of %.2f pF at %.3f MHz : %.1f kohm'\n",
    "      % (C_COUPLE * 1e12, F0 / 1e6, Xc / 1e3))\n",
    "print('  capacitive divider %.2f pF / (%.2f + %.1f) pF : %.4f  (%.1f dB)'\n",
    "      % (C_COUPLE * 1e12, C_COUPLE * 1e12, C_STRAY_EST * 1e12,\n",
    "         divider, 20 * np.log10(divider)))\n",
    "print('  -> every 10 mV across the tank arrives as %.3f mV at the board'\n",
    "      % (10.0 * divider))\n",
    "\n",
    "# resistive loading the pickup path puts across the tank:\n",
    "#   a series capacitor into a resistor R looks, from the tank, like a shunt\n",
    "#   resistance R (1 + (Xc/R)^2). With R = 1 Mohm and Xc = 13 kohm that is\n",
    "#   essentially R itself - i.e. the path is capacitive, not lossy.\n",
    "r_shunt = R_IN_BOARD * (1.0 + (Xc / R_IN_BOARD) ** 2)\n",
    "print('  equivalent shunt resistance across the tank : %.2f Mohm' % (r_shunt / 1e6))\n",
    "\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "print('MEASURED')\n",
    "peak_counts = float(np.sqrt(FIT['peak']))\n",
    "base_counts = float(np.sqrt(max(FIT['base'], 1e-300)))\n",
    "print('  peak response at resonance : %.1f counts (arb. units of the receiver)'\n",
    "      % peak_counts)\n",
    "print('  off-resonance baseline     : %.1f counts' % base_counts)\n",
    "print('  resonant contrast          : %.1f dB'\n",
    "      % (20 * np.log10(peak_counts / max(base_counts, 1e-300))))\n",
    "\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    gen.freq(F0); gen.amp(DRIVE_FRAC); gen.run(); time.sleep(0.05)\n",
    "    raw_peak = sc.peak_frac(SC_NMAX)\n",
    "finally:\n",
    "    gen.off()\n",
    "print('  raw input at resonance     : %.4f of full scale = %.2f mV peak'\n",
    "      % (raw_peak, 1e3 * raw_peak * V_FULLSCALE))\n",
    "\n",
    "# The one-way transfer of the whole analogue loop: out of the converter, through\n",
    "# the drive capacitor, through the coil at resonance, back through the pickup\n",
    "# capacitor and into the input. Step 8 needs exactly this number to know whether\n",
    "# a feedback sweep can show anything at all, and it is measured, not estimated.\n",
    "G_FWD = raw_peak / DRIVE_FRAC\n",
    "print('  one-way transfer DAC->ADC  : %.5f  (%.1f dB) at resonance'\n",
    "      % (G_FWD, 20 * np.log10(max(G_FWD, 1e-12))))\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- how much of that never went through the coil ---------------------------\n",
    "#  Drive far enough off resonance that the tank contributes nothing, and\n",
    "#  whatever still arrives came by another route. This is an independent check on\n",
    "#  the leak the Step 3 complex fit inferred, and the two should agree.\n",
    "_far = np.array([F0 - 40.0 * LW, F0 + 40.0 * LW])\n",
    "_far = _far[(_far > 1.0e6) & (_far < 0.45 * FS_CLK)]\n",
    "_ff, _zf = sweep(_far, drive_frac=DRIVE_FRAC, navg=N_AVG, level_guard=0.95)\n",
    "LEAK_DIRECT = float(np.mean(np.abs(_zf)))\n",
    "_on = float(FIT['amp_on'])\n",
    "LEAK_FRAC_DIRECT = LEAK_DIRECT / max(_on, 1e-300)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "print('LEAKAGE - signal arriving without going through the coil')\n",
    "print('  measured %+.0f linewidths off resonance : %.1f counts'\n",
    "      % (40.0, LEAK_DIRECT))\n",
    "print('  on-resonance response                  : %.1f counts' % _on)\n",
    "print('  leak / on-resonance                    : %.3f' % LEAK_FRAC_DIRECT)\n",
    "print('  leak / on-res, from the Step 3 fit     : %.3f' % LEAK_FRAC)\n",
    "\n",
    "# The resonant part of the transfer is what feedback actually acts on. Step 8\n",
    "# needs this, not the raw number above - using the raw one over-predicts the\n",
    "# loop gain by exactly the leak's share.\n",
    "# Power alone cannot split the on-resonance response into resonator and leak\n",
    "# AMPLITUDES - that needs the relative phase, and |z|^2 does not carry it. What\n",
    "# it does bound is the answer: if the leak is in phase the resonant part is\n",
    "# (1 - leak_frac) of the total, and if it is in quadrature it is\n",
    "# sqrt(1 - leak_frac^2), which is larger. Take the IN-PHASE value. It is the\n",
    "# smaller of the two, so it UNDER-predicts the loop gain rather than over - and\n",
    "# over-predicting is what manufactured a 4x \"shortfall\" out of nothing.\n",
    "G_FWD_RES = G_FWD * max(1.0 - LEAK_FRAC_DIRECT, 0.02)\n",
    "G_FWD_RES = float(min(G_FWD_RES, G_FWD))     # can never exceed the whole thing\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "print('  transfer that went through the coil    : %.5f  (%.1f dB)'\n",
    "      % (G_FWD_RES, 20 * np.log10(max(G_FWD_RES, 1e-12))))\n",
    "print('  -> Step 8 uses this. Feedback can only act on the part of the signal')\n",
    "print('     that actually came from the resonator.')\n",
    "if LEAK_FRAC_DIRECT > 0.3:\n",
    "    print('')\n",
    "    print('  This is a lot. The usual causes, in order: the two coax runs lying')\n",
    "    print('  against each other, a ground strap making a loop, or the coupling')\n",
    "    print('  capacitors being bridged by the layout. Separating the cables is')\n",
    "    print('  free and usually enough - do it and re-run Step 3 to see it fall.')\n",
    "if raw_peak < 0.01:\n",
    "    print('    -> under 1%% of full scale. Working, but only the top 7 of the')\n",
    "    print('       14 bits are doing anything. A short pickup lead or a')\n",
    "    print('       low-noise amplifier would buy back real resolution.')\n",
    "if raw_peak > FB_LEVEL_GUARD:\n",
    "    # A HARD STOP, not a warning. This is the first and only moment full drive\n",
    "    # sits exactly on resonance with a level actually measured, and everything\n",
    "    # after it (the linearity ladder in Step 6, the feedback in Step 8) drives\n",
    "    # at least this hard. If the front end is already this close to\n",
    "    # clipping there is no honest measurement further down, so stop here.\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError(\n",
    "        'input reached %.3f of full scale at resonance, above the %.2f guard. '\n",
    "        'LOWER DRIVE_FRAC (and DRIVE_MAX with it) and re-run from Step 3.'\n",
    "        % (raw_peak, FB_LEVEL_GUARD))\n",
    "\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "if L_EST is None:\n",
    "    print('THERMAL NOISE: skipped. Set L_EST in the configuration cell to the')\n",
    "    print('  coil inductance and re-run this cell to get the coil\\'s own Johnson')\n",
    "    print('  noise density and whether the board can see it unaided.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    kB = 1.380649e-23\n",
    "    r_par = Q_SWEEP * w0 * L_EST                 # tank equivalent parallel R\n",
    "    e_n = np.sqrt(4.0 * kB * T_COIL * r_par)     # V per root hertz at resonance\n",
    "    v_lsb = V_FULLSCALE / 8192.0\n",
    "    # 14-bit quantisation noise density spread over the first Nyquist zone:\n",
    "    e_board = (v_lsb / np.sqrt(12.0)) / np.sqrt(FS_CLK / 2.0)\n",
    "    print('THERMAL NOISE, using L = %.3f uH' % (L_EST * 1e6))\n",
    "    print('  tank equivalent parallel resistance : %.1f kohm' % (r_par / 1e3))\n",
    "    print('  coil Johnson noise at resonance     : %.1f nV/rtHz' % (e_n * 1e9))\n",
    "    print('  after the %.4f divider              : %.2f nV/rtHz'\n",
    "          % (divider, e_n * divider * 1e9))\n",
    "    print('  board quantisation floor            : %.2f nV/rtHz (ideal; the real'\n",
    "          % (e_board * 1e9))\n",
    "    print('                                         floor is higher - Step 2)')\n",
    "    ratio = (e_n * divider) / e_board\n",
    "    print('  ratio                               : %.1fx' % ratio)\n",
    "    if ratio < 3.0:\n",
    "        print('  -> the coil\\'s own noise is AT OR BELOW the board floor. Driven')\n",
    "        print('     measurements are fine; noise-driven ones need an amplifier.')\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print('  -> the coil\\'s own noise should be visible without an amplifier.')"
   ]
