   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "# Step 4b — The coil against its own inductance and capacitance\n",
    "\n",
    "Everything up to here has measured the coil **as a black box**: find a peak, fit a width, report\n",
    "a quality factor. This step is different, and it is the strongest test in the notebook, because\n",
    "`L` and `C` were measured *by a different instrument on a different day*. Two independent routes\n",
    "to the same number is the only real check available on a bench, and this is the one place the\n",
    "notebook has it.\n",
    "\n",
    "**The prediction.** A parallel tank sits at `f₀ = 1 / (2π√(LC))`. The capacitance across it is\n",
    "the coil's own `C_coil`, plus the `C_parallel` fitted to emulate the trap, plus the small\n",
    "contribution of the two coupling capacitors each in series with their cable. Nothing else is\n",
    "adjustable.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why the 39 pF matters more than it looks.** On its own, 423.5 nH with 1.59 pF resonates near\n",
    "**165 MHz** — above the 62.5 MHz Nyquist limit, so this board cannot see it *at all*, at any\n",
    "setting. The added capacitance is not a refinement of the model, it is what puts the resonance\n",
    "in the band. It also dominates the error budget: at 39 pF it is 25× the coil's own capacitance,\n",
    "so a 5% capacitor puts ±2.4% on the predicted centre frequency while the coil's ±3.8% on\n",
    "`C_coil` contributes ±0.07%. **If the prediction and the measurement disagree, suspect the\n",
    "capacitor's tolerance before suspecting the coil.**\n",
    "\n",
    "**The inversion is the deliverable.** Run it the other way — take the *measured* `f₀` and the\n",
    "*known* `L`, and solve for the total capacitance actually across the tank. Subtract what is\n",
    "accounted for, and what remains is the stray capacitance of the real assembly: the holder, the\n",
    "leads, the connectors. That number is the one worth carrying to the trap, and it cannot be got\n",
    "any other way.\n",
    "\n",
    "**And the losses.** With `L` known, the quality factor stops being dimensionless bookkeeping and\n",
    "becomes a resistance: `R_series = ω₀L/Q` is the coil's equivalent series resistance, and\n",
    "`R_parallel = Q·√(L/C)` is what the tank looks like at resonance — which is what sets both the\n",
    "signal budget of Step 4 and the loop gain of Step 8. Adding capacitance *lowers* both `f₀` and\n",
    "the characteristic impedance `√(L/C)`, so it costs quality factor and signal even though it\n",
    "changes nothing about the coil. Quantifying that cost is what makes this comparable with the\n",
    "bare-coil measurements taken before the capacitor went on.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  STEP 4b - THE COIL AGAINST ITS OWN L AND C\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "#  The only independent check in this notebook. L and C came from elsewhere; f0\n",
    "#  and Q came from Steps 3 and 5. Nothing here is fitted to anything above.\n",
    "# =============================================================================\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "print('STEP 4b - measured resonance against the known L and C')\n",
    "print('=' * 68)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- the capacitance actually across the tank -------------------------------\n",
    "#  Each coupling capacitor sits in series with everything after it, so what the\n",
    "#  tank sees from each port is the SERIES pair - and 0.3 pF in series with 30 pF\n",
    "#  is 0.297 pF, i.e. the small capacitor wins almost completely. Two ports, so\n",
    "#  it lands twice.\n",
    "C_SER_PORT = C_COUPLE * C_STRAY_EST / (C_COUPLE + C_STRAY_EST)\n",
    "C_PORTS = 2.0 * C_SER_PORT\n",
    "C_MODEL = C_COIL + C_PARALLEL + C_PORTS\n",
    "C_MODEL_ERR = np.sqrt(C_COIL_ERR ** 2 + C_PARALLEL_ERR ** 2)\n",
    "\n",
    "def _f_of(L, Cq):\n",
    "    return 1.0 / (2.0 * np.pi * np.sqrt(L * Cq))\n",
    "\n",
    "F0_PRED = _f_of(L_COIL, C_MODEL)\n",
    "# f0 goes as (LC)^-1/2, so a fractional error in L or C becomes HALF of one in f0\n",
    "F0_PRED_ERR = F0_PRED * 0.5 * np.hypot(L_COIL_ERR / L_COIL, C_MODEL_ERR / C_MODEL)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('capacitance across the tank')\n",
    "print('  coil self-capacitance      : %6.2f +/- %.2f pF' % (C_COIL * 1e12, C_COIL_ERR * 1e12))\n",
    "print('  fitted parallel capacitor  : %6.2f +/- %.2f pF'\n",
    "      % (C_PARALLEL * 1e12, C_PARALLEL_ERR * 1e12))\n",
    "print('  two coupling ports         : %6.2f pF  (%.3f pF each: %.1f pF in series with %.0f pF)'\n",
    "      % (C_PORTS * 1e12, C_SER_PORT * 1e12, C_COUPLE * 1e12, C_STRAY_EST * 1e12))\n",
    "print('  ---------------------------------------')\n",
    "print('  total, modelled            : %6.2f +/- %.2f pF' % (C_MODEL * 1e12, C_MODEL_ERR * 1e12))\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- would this even be visible without the added capacitor? ----------------\n",
    "F0_BARE = _f_of(L_COIL, C_COIL + C_PORTS)\n",
    "print('without the %.0f pF the coil would sit at %.1f MHz' % (C_PARALLEL * 1e12, F0_BARE / 1e6))\n",
    "if F0_BARE > 0.5 * FS_CLK:\n",
    "    print('  -> above the %.1f MHz Nyquist limit. The added capacitance is what'\n",
    "          % (0.5 * FS_CLK / 1e6))\n",
    "    print('     makes this measurable at all; it is not a correction.')\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- prediction against measurement -----------------------------------------\n",
    "_dev = F0 - F0_PRED\n",
    "_sig = abs(_dev) / F0_PRED_ERR if F0_PRED_ERR > 0 else float('inf')\n",
    "print('centre frequency')\n",
    "print('  predicted from L and C     : %.3f +/- %.3f MHz'\n",
    "      % (F0_PRED / 1e6, F0_PRED_ERR / 1e6))\n",
    "print('  measured (Step 3)          : %.3f MHz' % (F0 / 1e6))\n",
    "print('  difference                 : %+.3f MHz  (%+.2f%%, %.1f sigma)'\n",
    "      % (_dev / 1e6, 100 * _dev / F0_PRED, _sig))\n",
    "if _sig <= 2.0 and abs(_dev) / F0_PRED <= 0.02:\n",
    "    print('  AGREE - two independent routes to the same resonance')\n",
    "elif _sig <= 2.0:\n",
    "    print('  WITHIN THE ERROR BAR, BUT ONLY BECAUSE THE ERROR BAR IS WIDE.')\n",
    "    print('  %+.1f%% is a real offset; it passes only because the %.0f pF part is'\n",
    "          % (100 * _dev / F0_PRED, C_PARALLEL * 1e12))\n",
    "    print('  assumed to +-%.0f%%. Measure that capacitor and re-run - the'\n",
    "          % (100 * C_PARALLEL_ERR / C_PARALLEL))\n",
    "    print('  inversion below is the sharper test and it disagrees.')\n",
    "elif _sig <= 4.0:\n",
    "    print('  MARGINAL. Before blaming the coil, check the tolerance of the %.0f pF'\n",
    "          % (C_PARALLEL * 1e12))\n",
    "    print('  part: it is %.0fx the coil capacitance, so it dominates the prediction.'\n",
    "          % (C_PARALLEL / C_COIL))\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('  DISAGREE. In order of likelihood: the parallel capacitor is not the')\n",
    "    print('  value marked on it; there is more stray capacitance in the assembly')\n",
    "    print('  than C_STRAY_EST allows; L was measured at a very different frequency')\n",
    "    print('  from %.1f MHz and the coil is not behaving as a simple inductor here.'\n",
    "          % (F0 / 1e6))\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- the inversion: what capacitance is REALLY across the tank ---------------\n",
    "#  This is the number to carry forward. f0 and L are both known, so C follows,\n",
    "#  and whatever it exceeds the model by is stray capacitance in the real\n",
    "#  assembly - holder, leads, connectors - which nothing else here can measure.\n",
    "C_IMPLIED = 1.0 / (L_COIL * (2.0 * np.pi * F0) ** 2)\n",
    "C_IMPLIED_ERR = C_IMPLIED * (L_COIL_ERR / L_COIL)\n",
    "C_UNACCOUNTED = C_IMPLIED - C_MODEL\n",
    "print('inverting: total capacitance implied by the measured f0 and the known L')\n",
    "print('  implied C_total            : %6.2f +/- %.2f pF'\n",
    "      % (C_IMPLIED * 1e12, C_IMPLIED_ERR * 1e12))\n",
    "print('  modelled C_total           : %6.2f +/- %.2f pF' % (C_MODEL * 1e12, C_MODEL_ERR * 1e12))\n",
    "print('  unaccounted for            : %+6.2f pF' % (C_UNACCOUNTED * 1e12))\n",
    "if C_UNACCOUNTED > 2.0 * C_MODEL_ERR:\n",
    "    print('  -> real stray capacitance in the assembly. Carry this to the trap:')\n",
    "    print('     the holder and leads contribute %.1f pF and the trap build will'\n",
    "          % (C_UNACCOUNTED * 1e12))\n",
    "    print('     see something similar.')\n",
    "elif C_UNACCOUNTED < -2.0 * C_MODEL_ERR:\n",
    "    print('  -> NEGATIVE, which is not physical: something in the model is too')\n",
    "    print('     large. The parallel capacitor being under its marked value is the')\n",
    "    print('     usual answer; a high reading of L is the other.')\n",
    "elif C_UNACCOUNTED < -0.5:\n",
    "    print('  -> NEGATIVE BY %.2f pF, WHICH IS NOT PHYSICAL. Stray capacitance can'\n",
    "          % abs(C_UNACCOUNTED * 1e12))\n",
    "    print('     only add. Something in the model is too big, and the %.0f pF part'\n",
    "          % (C_PARALLEL * 1e12))\n",
    "    print('     is 25x the coil capacitance, so it is the first suspect: measure')\n",
    "    print('     it. A high reading of L is the other. Do not carry the implied')\n",
    "    print('     total forward until this is resolved.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('  -> consistent with zero. The assembly adds no measurable stray.')\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- losses, now that L is a number -----------------------------------------\n",
    "W0 = 2.0 * np.pi * F0\n",
    "Z0_TANK = np.sqrt(L_COIL / C_IMPLIED)\n",
    "R_SERIES = W0 * L_COIL / Q_SWEEP\n",
    "R_PARALLEL = Q_SWEEP * W0 * L_COIL\n",
    "print('losses, from Q = %.1f and L = %.1f nH' % (Q_SWEEP, L_COIL * 1e9))\n",
    "print('  characteristic impedance   : %.1f ohm   (sqrt(L/C))' % Z0_TANK)\n",
    "print('  series resistance (ESR)    : %.3f ohm' % R_SERIES)\n",
    "print('  parallel resistance        : %.1f kohm  (the tank at resonance)'\n",
    "      % (R_PARALLEL / 1e3))\n",
    "print('  linewidth implied by Q     : %.1f kHz' % (F0 / Q_SWEEP / 1e3))\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- the cost of the added capacitor ----------------------------------------\n",
    "#  The capacitor does not change the coil's series resistance, and Q = w0 L / Rs,\n",
    "#  so Q simply follows f0 down. That is what makes this run comparable with any\n",
    "#  measurement taken before the capacitor went on.\n",
    "Q_BARE_IMPLIED = Q_SWEEP * F0_BARE / F0\n",
    "print('what the %.0f pF costs' % (C_PARALLEL * 1e12))\n",
    "print('  Q here                     : %.1f at %.2f MHz' % (Q_SWEEP, F0 / 1e6))\n",
    "print('  implied bare-coil Q        : %.0f at %.1f MHz  (same ESR, Q scales with f0)'\n",
    "      % (Q_BARE_IMPLIED, F0_BARE / 1e6))\n",
    "print('  characteristic impedance   : %.0f -> %.0f ohm'\n",
    "      % (np.sqrt(L_COIL / (C_COIL + C_PORTS)), Z0_TANK))\n",
    "print('  -> the capacitor costs a factor %.1f in both Q and tank impedance.'\n",
    "      % (F0_BARE / F0))\n",
    "print('     Compare Q against an earlier bare-coil measurement using the implied')\n",
    "print('     value above, not the one measured here.')\n",
    "print('')\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---- does the measured loop transfer match the model? -----------------------\n",
    "#  G_FWD was measured in Step 4. Predict it from the tank impedance and the two\n",
    "#  capacitors, and compare. A measured value well ABOVE the prediction means\n",
    "#  signal is reaching the input by some route other than the pickup capacitor -\n",
    "#  the two coax runs coupling to each other is the usual one - and that route\n",
    "#  has its own phase, which would corrupt Step 8's axis.\n",
    "_Xc = 1.0 / (W0 * C_COUPLE)\n",
    "_v_tank = R_PARALLEL / np.hypot(_Xc, R_PARALLEL)\n",
    "_div = C_COUPLE / (C_COUPLE + C_STRAY_EST)\n",
    "G_FWD_PRED = _v_tank * _div\n",
    "print('forward transfer DAC -> coil -> ADC')\n",
    "print('  drive side: %.1f kohm of reactance into a %.1f kohm tank -> %.3f'\n",
    "      % (_Xc / 1e3, R_PARALLEL / 1e3, _v_tank))\n",
    "print('  pickup divider                                          -> %.5f' % _div)\n",
    "print('  predicted G_FWD            : %.5f  (%.1f dB)'\n",
    "      % (G_FWD_PRED, 20 * np.log10(max(G_FWD_PRED, 1e-12))))\n",
    "print('  measured G_FWD (Step 4)    : %.5f  (%.1f dB)'\n",
    "      % (G_FWD, 20 * np.log10(max(G_FWD, 1e-12))))\n",
    "print('  measured / predicted       : %.2fx' % (G_FWD / max(G_FWD_PRED, 1e-12)))\n",
    "if G_FWD > 3.0 * G_FWD_PRED:\n",
    "    print('  -> MORE signal arrives than the capacitors can explain. Something is')\n",
    "    print('     coupling around them: the two coax runs lying together, or the')\n",
    "    print('     ground strap. It carries its own phase, so Step 8 phase axis is')\n",
    "    print('     suspect until it is found. Separate the cables and re-run.')\n",
    "elif G_FWD < 0.33 * G_FWD_PRED:\n",
    "    print('  -> LESS signal than predicted. Suspect the coupling capacitors being')\n",
    "    print('     smaller than marked, or more cable capacitance than C_STRAY_EST.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('  -> consistent with coupling through the capacitors alone.')\n"
   ]
