   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "# Step 5 — A second, independent width\n",
    "\n",
    "The discipline that replaces a known answer is **measuring the same quantity two ways that fail\n",
    "differently**. Agreement makes a number believable; disagreement tells you something is wrong\n",
    "before you build on it.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Why it is no longer the phase\n",
    "\n",
    "Earlier versions took the second width from the *phase* of the swept response. On this board\n",
    "that cannot work, and it is worth understanding why rather than tuning the fit until it stops\n",
    "complaining.\n",
    "\n",
    "`sweep()` retunes two independent numerically-controlled oscillators for every point: the\n",
    "generator's, by writing its frequency word, and the receiver's local oscillator, by writing\n",
    "another. The two are locked in *frequency* — the local-oscillator word is exactly four times the\n",
    "generator's step, so once both are running their phase difference is constant. But they are\n",
    "retuned by **two separate register writes**, and between those writes the generator is already\n",
    "at the new frequency while the local oscillator is still at the old one. The phase that opens up\n",
    "in that gap is\n",
    "\n",
    "    Δφ = 2π · (f_new − f_old) · Δt\n",
    "\n",
    "and it never closes — it accumulates from point to point. With a 18 kHz grid step and Python\n",
    "taking tens of microseconds between two register writes, that is **radians per point**, growing\n",
    "linearly across the sweep. It looks exactly like a transport delay of tens of microseconds,\n",
    "which is why the delay fit ran to the end of its range and reported 1500 ns, the largest value\n",
    "it was allowed to consider.\n",
    "\n",
    "Worse, `Δt` is *jittery*. The ramp is not reproducible, so it cannot be calibrated out, and the\n",
    "scatter it leaves is a large fraction of a turn per point. The phase between one sweep point and\n",
    "the next is simply not a measurement on this board.\n",
    "\n",
    "Two consequences, both now built in. Every fit in this notebook uses `|z|²` only. And the\n",
    "leakage that motivated the phase fit is instead recovered from the **asymmetry** of the power\n",
    "lineshape, which carries the same information and survives the retune.\n",
    "\n",
    "*Fixing it properly would mean sweeping without retuning — parking both oscillators and stepping\n",
    "the frequency in the fabric, or resetting the acquisition chain at every point so the local\n",
    "oscillator restarts from a known phase (`red_pitaya_acq.v` does reset it on `CTRL[1]`). Neither\n",
    "is a change to this notebook.*\n",
    "\n",
    "## What replaces it\n",
    "\n",
    "**Measure the width with a different receiver.** The decimation sets the receiver's clean\n",
    "window, and a window that is not small compared with the linewidth broadens what it measures.\n",
    "Repeat the fit at twice the decimation — half the window — and a real width does not move. One\n",
    "that does was being set by the instrument, not by the coil.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is genuinely independent in the way that matters: it changes the filter chain, the output\n",
    "rate and the averaging, while leaving the coil alone.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
