    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "# Step 7 — Does anything move while you are measuring?\n",
    "\n",
    "The emulated coil was exactly constant for as long as you cared to look. A real one is not: it\n",
    "answers to room temperature, to airflow, and to anything mechanical. A full feedback map takes\n",
    "several minutes, and if the centre moves during the scan the map smears in a way that looks\n",
    "like real structure.\n",
    "\n",
    "This revisits the same measurement at intervals and reports two different things, which are\n",
    "easy to conflate and matter for different reasons:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Drift** — a slow, one-way trend. It biases a long scan. Measured as the straight-line\n",
    "  slope over the whole run.\n",
    "- **Scatter** — point-to-point wobble. It sets the floor on any single measurement. Measured\n",
    "  as the deviation about that line.\n",
    "\n",
    "Both are reported *in linewidths*, because that is the unit in which they either matter or do\n",
    "not. A drift of a hundredth of a linewidth over ten minutes is irrelevant; a tenth is not."
   ]
